<h2 id="linernotes">Liner notes</h2>

<h3>Less than a Pearl</h3>
<p>"...yet there is one sound that is not their own and which their hearts yearn to have. It is the sound of the <strong>Song of the Loxians</strong>."</p>
<p>"It is a sound that awakens in <strong>Valley-dwellers</strong> a strange feeling, one they cannot know yet one that is more familiar to them than their own heartbeat."</p>
<p>"And it awakens in the hearts of all the Valley-dwellers a longing that brings them to the edge of tears, because it is the song of both the <strong>beginning and the end</strong>..."</p>

<h3>Amarantine</h3>
<p>The word <strong>Amarantine</strong> was previously referenced in the song <strong>"Flora's Secret"</strong> on <em>A Day Without Rain</em>, where it was spelled as "amaranthine".</p>
<p>In that earlier track, the word signified the color purple and the eyes of a flower looking up toward the heavens.</p>

<h3>Everlasting Love</h3>
<p>In this title song, <strong>Amarantine</strong> takes on the ancient Greek definition meaning <strong>"everlasting"</strong> or <strong>"immortal"</strong>.</p>
<p>It stands as a deeply personal composition centered entirely around the concept of <strong>eternal love</strong>.</p>

<h3>It's in the rain</h3>
<p>A small oasis. A harbour. A haven.</p>
<p>The soothing sound of falling rain calms the mind, opening quiet moments for <strong>reflection and imagination</strong>.</p>

<h3>If I could be where you are</h3>
<p>This is a song of profound sadness, capturing the sorrow of not knowing where a missing loved one is or how to find them.</p>
<p>It stands as a dedicated anthem for <strong>the missing</strong> throughout the world.</p>

<h3>The River Sings</h3>
<p>This track forms part of the Loxian trilogy originating from Roma Ryan's book <strong><em>Water Shows the Hidden Heart</em></strong>.</p>
<p>Sung in <strong>Loxian</strong>, it describes people sending their words out into the night sky, wondering if they will ever find other life in space.</p>

<h3>Long Long Journey</h3>
<p>Though one may travel to faraway places, wide oceans, and foreign lands, the heart desires nothing more than to return home.</p>
<p>Physical miles across the sea mean nothing to a heart that is on its <strong>journey home</strong>.</p>

<h3>Sumiregusa</h3>
<p>The lyrics are inspired by a classic <strong>hokku poem</strong> by Japanese poet <strong>Matsuo Bashō</strong>, written during his travels to Otsu.</p>
<p>In his verse, Bashō described how his heart leaped with delight upon discovering a <strong>wild violet</strong> along a rugged mountain road.</p>

<h3>Epihanies in Nature</h3>
<p>This track celebrates those intense moments when human beings feel deeply moved by an encounter with the natural world.</p>
<p>It represents a quiet personal epiphany and a joyful <strong>celebration of life</strong>.</p>

<h3>Someone said goodbye</h3>
<p>Everywhere across the globe, life unfolds for everyone in different ways.</p>
<p>When the day draws to a close, quiet reflection can bring the saddest moments back to mind, a feeling captured in this song.</p>

<h3>A Moment Lost</h3>
<p>Words written in the sand disappear as the ocean tide washes in and erases them completely.</p>
<p>However, harsh words spoken in anger by a loved one remain etched in the hidden corners of the heart.</p>

<h3>Forgiveness and Healing</h3>
<p>These painful words echo through the night until gentle words arrive to comfort, heal, and <strong>restore love</strong>.</p>

<p>It is a song of regret over words uttered in haste, and a celebration of words that bring <strong>forgiveness</strong>.</p>

<h3>Amid the falling snow</h3>
<p>"And the air was filled with feathers..."</p>
<p>This song recalls the childhood enchantment of watching <strong>falling snow</strong> for the first time during Christmastide.</p>
<p>It honors those who retain their sense of wonder and magic as they grow older.</p>

<h3>Water shows the hidden heart</h3>
<p>This composition tells the story of a man searching across symbolic cities, islands, and valleys for the love he has lost.</p>
<p>His emotional journey takes on physical forms, adapted from Roma Ryan's book of the same title.</p>

<h3>Reflections of the Soul</h3>
<p>"...he looks into the eyes of the water and sees his own eyes, looking."</p>
<p>"They reflect everything, these waters, even the <strong>hidden heart</strong>."</p>

